s=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">thinly sliced ribeye steak</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">hoagie rolls</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">6</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">slices</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">provolone cheese</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">large</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">piece</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">green bell pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">minced</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt and pepper</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7276-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7276\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Large skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the steak and vegetables.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7276-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7276-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7276\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add sliced onion, bell pepper, and minced garlic; sauté until softened, about 5 minutes.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Season ribeye slices with salt and pepper and add to the skillet; cook until browned, about 4–5 minutes.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Divide meat and vegetables into four portions in the skillet.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Top each portion with 1–2 slices of provolone and cover until cheese melts, about 2 minutes.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Slice hoagie rolls, toast lightly if desired, and fill each with a cheesy steak mixture.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7276-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Serve hot and enjoy your homemade Philly Cheesesteak!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-7276-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>500</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>40g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up a delicious <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheesesteak\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Philly Cheesesteak</a> with these easy-to-find ingredients!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Philly-Cheesesteak.webp\" alt=\"A collection of fresh ingredients for making a Philly Cheesesteak, including ribeye steak, hoagie rolls, provolone cheese, onion, bell pepper, garlic, and olive oil.\" class=\"wp-image-7274\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Philly-Cheesesteak.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Philly-Cheesesteak-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 lb</strong> – thinly sliced ribeye steak</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>4</strong> – hoagie rolls</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>6 slices</strong> – provolone cheese</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1</strong> – large onion</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1</strong> – green bell pepper</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cloves</strong> – garlic</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp</strong> – olive oil</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt and pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-philly-cheesesteak\"><strong>How to Make Philly Cheesesteak</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up a delicious Philly Cheesesteak! This recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare and 15 minutes to cook, making it a quick and satisfying meal. Let’s dive into the cheesy goodness!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Philly-Cheesesteak-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide to making a Philly Cheesesteak, showcasing the cooking process from sautéing vegetables to filling hoagie rolls.\" class=\"wp-image-7275\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Philly-Cheesesteak-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Philly-Cheesesteak-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Heat the Skillet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Sauté the Veggies</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add sliced onion, bell pepper, and minced garlic; sauté until softened, about 5 minutes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cook the Meat</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season ribeye slices with salt and pepper and add to the skillet; cook until browned, about 4–5 minutes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Portion It Out</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Divide meat and vegetables into four portions in the skillet.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Melt the Cheese</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Top each portion with 1–2 slices of provolone and cover until cheese melts, about 2 minutes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Prepare the Rolls</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Slice hoagie rolls, toast lightly if desired, and fill each with a cheesy steak mixture.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Serve and Enjoy!</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve hot and enjoy your homemade Philly Cheesesteak!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Not specified</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and cheesy</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-philly-cheesesteak\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Philly Cheesesteak</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose ribeye steak for the best flavor and tenderness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Slice the meat thinly against the grain for a melt-in-your-mouth texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a mix of provolone and mozzarella for a creamy, delicious cheese blend.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toast the hoagie rolls lightly for added crunch and warmth.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t rush the sautéing of onions and peppers; caramelization adds depth of flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-philly-cheesesteak\"><strong>How to Serve this Philly Cheesesteak</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with crispy French fries for a classic combo.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a side of tangy coleslaw for a refreshing crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with sautéed mushrooms and onions for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of creamy ranch or zesty barbecue sauce for dipping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in lettuce for a low-carb twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve on a toasted hoagie roll for that authentic feel.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Complement with a side of pickles for a tangy bite.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try with sweet potato fries for a delicious alternative.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your Philly Cheesesteak later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Philly Cheesesteak Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow leftovers to cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Philly Cheesesteak</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap individual portions tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped portions in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and type of dish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 2 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Philly Cheesesteak</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat for best texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of beef broth or water to keep it moist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat until warmed through, about 5-7 minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is typically on a Philly cheesesteak?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A classic Philly cheesesteak typically includes thinly sliced beefsteak, sautéed onions, and melted cheese, all served on a long hoagie roll. Some variations may also include toppings like bell peppers or mushrooms, but the traditional version keeps it simple with just the meat, cheese, and onions for that authentic flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is the secret to a good Philly cheesesteak?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The secret to a good Philly cheesesteak lies in the quality of the ingredients and the cooking technique. Using fresh, high-quality beef and cheese, along with properly sautéed onions, can make a huge difference. Additionally, cooking the meat on a flat-top grill allows for that perfect sear and flavor infusion, creating a deliciously satisfying sandwich.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the secret ingredient in Philly cheesesteak?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While there isn&#8217;t a single secret ingredient, many chefs swear by using a good quality cheese, like provolone or Cheez Whiz, to elevate the flavor. Some also add a dash of Worcestershire sauce or a sprinkle of garlic powder to enhance the overall taste, giving it that extra kick that makes a Philly cheesesteak unforgettable.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Which cheese is best for Philly cheesesteaks?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best cheese for a Philly cheesesteak is often a matter of personal preference, but traditional choices include provolone, American cheese, and Cheez Whiz. Provolone offers a nice balance of flavor and melt, while Cheez Whiz provides that creamy, nostalgic taste that many fans love. Experimenting with different cheeses can help you find your perfect combination!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There you have it, the ultimate Philly Cheesesteak! This dish is not just a meal; it&#8217;s a warm hug on a plate. So gather your ingredients, channel your inner chef, and enjoy the simple pleasure of creating something delicious. Trust me, every bite will take you back to the streets of Philly. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
